The lessons help your smart helper know what to do better tomorrow.
So every day the helper gets a little better at helping you.
That's an Intelligence Report.
It is your story becoming intelligence — and your intelligence helping write the next part of your story.

4. GRANDMA
Think of it like a really good household ledger combined with a thoughtful yearly journal.
You don't just want a pile of receipts.
You want to know:
Where did we spend our time? What did we accomplish? What did we learn? What problems kept coming up? What worked? What didn't? What should we do differently?
The daily report gives you the day's picture.
